        {
          "handle": "eliebakouch",
          "creator": "@eliebakouch",
          "text": "wrong text: \"here is the final mixture, 50%+ code is quite high but that makes sense. also you can see that some mix percentages look relatively close to the target loss: 55% code final mix - 50% weight in target loss, 15% for stem - 17.5% target loss. not the case for math tho mid-training mixture increases stem and math to 35%\"",
          "link": "https://nitter.net/eliebakouch/status/2061998671856640327#m",
          "date_utc": "2026-06-03T02:29:28+00:00",
          "is_curated": false,
          "org": "",
          "image_urls": [],
          "articles": []
        },
        {
          "handle": "eliebakouch",
          "creator": "@eliebakouch",
          "text": "the entropy based clipping is pretty cool, it keeps the model's entropy around 0.3 which seems to be their sweet spot, but we add a pretty crucial HP here imo",
          "link": "https://nitter.net/eliebakouch/status/2061998120842543396#m",
          "date_utc": "2026-06-03T02:27:16+00:00",
          "is_curated": false,
          "org": "",
          "image_urls": [
            "https://nitter.net/pic/media%2FHJ2wBmQXAAAe4M0.jpg"
          ],
          "articles": []
        },
        {
          "handle": "eliebakouch",
          "creator": "@eliebakouch",
          "text": "length penalty is very elegant and simple tbh",
          "link": "https://nitter.net/eliebakouch/status/2061997579336912951#m",
          "date_utc": "2026-06-03T02:25:07+00:00",
          "is_curated": false,
